{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th","id":1506480,"title":"icv2, Fall 2022: VtM comes 4th !","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-26T07:50:21-07:00","id":1506480,"title":"icv2, Fall 2022: VtM comes 4th !","content":"Quite unexpectedly, Vampire: The Masquerade has nearly reached the top 3 in the icv2 sales chart last Fall, as it came 4th in reported and estimated sales by retailers, producers and distributors.<br /> <br /> Vampire was surpassed by dnd 5e (of course), Pathfinder, and the combined 5E OGL lines: considering the last months mostly saw reprints of Cults and Chicago supplements, this is a really interesting result.<br /> <br /> Let's see whether the Player's Guide, Blood Sigils and Werewolf 5e will help the Wod stay up in the next charts!<br /> <br /> Link here: <u><a href=\"https://icv2.com/articles/markets/view/53650/top-hobby-channel-roleplaying-games-fall-2022\" target=\"_blank\">https://icv2.com/articles/markets/vi...ames-fall-2022</a></u><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T08:08:30-07:00","id":1506483,"title":"","content":"that's wonderful to hear!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T08:41:41-07:00","id":1506485,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting data-point but I think it has less to do with VtM and the WOD and more to do with Renegade.<br /> <br /> A couple things:<ul><li>This only covers the Fall and considering the buying-habits you get with RPG-books looking at the whole year is a better indicator</li> <li>BUT... it shows that Renegade's partnership with Hasbro continues to pay off (I mean, Transformers at #4 is more impressive in my opinion)</li> <li>In 2021, if I remember correctly all the other licensed RPGs from Renegade (GI Joe, Transformers and Power Rangers) sold better than Vampire but again... they are partnering with Hasbro there</li> <li>H5 is nowhere to be seen</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T08:49:45-07:00","id":1506486,"title":"","content":"There's a reason Renegade is the distributor: also, distribution by itself guarantees nothing, if the product isn't sound.<br /> <br /> Apparently, there's a purchasing fanbase out there that doesn't think the boat is sinking. <br /> <br /> I really doubt H5 was ever intended to get into the &quot;top5&quot; selling chart of RPGs, so I wouldn't take this as a metric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T09:07:12-07:00","id":1506487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506486#post1506486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason Renegade is the distributor: also, distribution by itself guarantees nothing, if the product isn't sound.<br /> <br /> Apparently, there's a purchasing fanbase out there that doesn't think the boat is sinking.<br /> <br /> I really doubt H5 was ever intended to get into the &quot;top5&quot; selling chart of RPGs, so I wouldn't take this as a metric.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, another thing you have to keep in mind there, though, is the distribution in percentage between #1,#2, # 3 5E OGL and the rest. There's a big gulf between the amount of books D&amp;D (including 5E OGL) and Pathfinder sell and a <i>huge </i>gulf between what those are selling compared to the rest. VtM being at #4 is in a very different league compared to the three before.<br /> <br /> And quality is less relevant here than name-recognition. That's the whole business-model for Renegade it seems. I looked at the Power Rangers RPG and it wasn't great; words like &quot;uninspired&quot; and &quot;bog-standard&quot; came to mind when I read it. Being connected to Hasbro puts them in a really good place when it comes to distribution as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T09:44:51-07:00","id":1506489,"title":"","content":"It's not strange that D&amp;D (including 5E OGL) and Pathfinder outsold VtM - they are competing at totally different numbers and capacity - but it's more interesting that VtM outsold the likes of Cthulhu, Cyberpunk, Shadowrun etc without new manuals coming out.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is just a quarterly bullettin, but it still a signal that VtM is maintaining a market relevance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T09:56:21-07:00","id":1506490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506489#post1506489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not strange that D&amp;D (including 5E OGL) and Pathfinder outsold VtM - they are competing at totally different numbers and capacity - but it's more interesting that VtM outsold the likes of Cthulhu, Cyberpunk, Shadowrun etc without new manuals coming out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would chalk that up to the limited time-frame here plus Renegade's distribution-prowess by partnering with Hasbro (as I said, Transformers is the more impressive one on that chart, I think). If you were looking at 2022 in total, VtM probably would be on # 8 or less. The icv2-reports also take Kickstarters into consideration and if you're looking at the whole year then, I'd wager VtM is <i>nowhere close</i> to where the Avatar RPG is charting.<br /> <br /> I think looking at this report isn't really enough to say anything conclusively about VtM. Especially because my take is that Renegade's distribution-prowess in partnership with Hasbro while having all these licensed RPGs is more relevant here than anything VtM-specific. The accessibility/availability of VtM-books in stores helps VtM (especially in light of the supply-chain-troubles of recent years due to the pandemic) but this is an external factor helping VtM and not VtM as a brand having some kind of cultural resurgence/newfound popularity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T10:44:39-07:00","id":1506494,"title":"","content":"Makes you wonder what would happen if Paradox hooked Onyx Path up with better distribution resources for CofD and Exalted...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T10:53:02-07:00","id":1506495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506494#post1506494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes you wonder what would happen if Paradox hooked Onyx Path up with better distribution resources for CofD and Exalted...</div> </div> </div> </div>wouldn't that be mighty expenseive for everyone involved? but i hope they can do so","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T11:46:49-07:00","id":1506505,"title":"","content":"There are significant up front costs that keeps Onyx Path from doing it themselves yes... but considering those properties are owned by Paradox and if wider distribution would net greater sales it would profit them in the long run... it means both properties become options for Paradox to use for things like video games and so on by building up from the existing player base.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T11:50:08-07:00","id":1506506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506505#post1506505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are significant up front costs that keeps Onyx Path from doing it themselves yes... but considering those properties are owned by Paradox and if wider distribution would net greater sales it would profit them in the long run... it means both properties become options for Paradox to use for things like video games and so on by building up from the existing player base.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah,gosh i wish i knew why they haven't done that yet,maybe it just bad bussiness decisions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T11:53:29-07:00","id":1506508,"title":"","content":"For the CofD, one could at least understand the logic of not trying to hype up both it and the WoD at the same time (even if I think evidence goes against that conclusion).<br /> <br /> Leaving Exalted in the lurch? No idea why they'd do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T11:59:24-07:00","id":1506510,"title":"","content":"I mean, in this case, what I'm even more interested in is to see how Renegade's partnership with Hasbro develops from now on. Because Hasbro is in a tight spot right now. The whole OGL-thing with D&amp;D started out by the Bank Of America complaining about Magic underperforming and then you had that fireside-chat with the infamous phrase of &quot;D&amp;D is under-monetized&quot;. Next thing you know the whole OGL-thing got leaked and well... here we are. That's another reason not to take this particular report too seriously. The RPG-market-situation has changed since last Fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T12:23:16-07:00","id":1506514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506490#post1506490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would chalk that up to the limited time-frame here plus Renegade's distribution-prowess by partnering with Hasbro (as I said, Transformers is the more impressive one on that chart, I think). If you were looking at 2022 in total, VtM probably would be on # 8 or less. The icv2-reports also take Kickstarters into consideration and if you're looking at the whole year then, I'd wager VtM is <i>nowhere close</i> to where the Avatar RPG is charting.<br /> <br /> I think looking at this report isn't really enough to say anything conclusively about VtM. Especially because my take is that Renegade's distribution-prowess in partnership with Hasbro while having all these licensed RPGs is more relevant here than anything VtM-specific. The accessibility/availability of VtM-books in stores helps VtM (especially in light of the supply-chain-troubles of recent years due to the pandemic) but this is an external factor helping VtM and not VtM as a brand having some kind of cultural resurgence/newfound popularity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the last time V5 charted was back in 2019 so as there were no new releases round September last year it was likely due to the big backlog of folks picking up print run copies of Chicago and Blood Gods when they became available that quarter. Looking at the previous quarter 4 and 5 were also Renegade properties which does seem to indicate that at least for the moment their share of the market is fairly secure. I'd wager for the next quarter Renegade will also be there likely due to Avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T16:48:04-07:00","id":1506545,"title":"","content":"Avatar is Magpie, not Renegade.<br /> <br /> It's really interesting to see how all these new licensed properties have gotten a solid sales start, even if the reviews of the system are rather lacklustre. I hope all three of them were good sellers and the people that enjoy them get a couple of years of support.<br /> <br /> As for VtM popping up, that's nice - I assume it's due to the reprints of the Renegade books since this is the first time they released things that were under different umbrellas? I'm really keen to see what the impact of the new books will be in the coming quarters.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T02:06:35-07:00","id":1506616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506545#post1506545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avatar is Magpie, not Renegade.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Why did I think it was Renegade? Getting old.....or I read someone else who made the same mistake...<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T10:51:31-07:00","id":1506644,"title":"","content":"I always thought VTM was just after the bread and butter books, so I guess that's the case. I wonder if all the recent videogame releases have been bringing in new fans and players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","name":"ShovelHeart3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27842_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T13:00:13-07:00","id":1506651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506494#post1506494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes you wonder what would happen if Paradox hooked Onyx Path up with better distribution resources for CofD and Exalted...</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox doesn't have anything to do with the distribution resources though. That's literally why they hired Renegade when Modiphius was dropped, because RGS has those distribution resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T16:53:07-07:00","id":1506669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShovelHeart3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506644#post1506644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought VTM was just after the bread and butter books, so I guess that's the case. I wonder if all the recent videogame releases have been bringing in new fans and players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but they didn't go over well with video game audiences, aside from perhaps the Bloodhunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T17:12:35-07:00","id":1506673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506669#post1506669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly, but they didn't go over well with video game audiences, aside from perhaps the Bloodhunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoyed all of the visual novel games, but you're right. At least Bloodlines is still a classic that regularly gets covered by YTers and such. I really hope they don't drop the ball on Bloodlines 2......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27842-shovelheart3","name":"ShovelHeart3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27842_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T17:17:56-07:00","id":1506674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506651#post1506651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Paradox doesn't have anything to do with the distribution resources though. That's literally why they hired Renegade when Modiphius was dropped, because RGS has those distribution resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>How, exactly, do you think RGS is selling OPP made V5 books? Because I don't think Paradox has nothing to do with that, and Paradox as the owners of the IPs, could make that happen for CofD and Exalted too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T17:42:56-07:00","id":1506677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506674#post1506674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How, exactly, do you think RGS is selling OPP made V5 books? Because I don't think Paradox has nothing to do with that, and Paradox as the owners of the IPs, could make that happen for CofD and Exalted too.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was that Paradox didn't set up the distribution stuff, that's RGS' own thing that they do separate from their Paradox contract (they have plenty of other stuff they distro). What you posted sounded like 'if PDX set up distribution channels for OPP' which, well, they wouldn't do. That's why they've sought out licensing partners who *already* have that stuff in place. Sure, they could let RGS print stuff, but that wasn't the content or context of what was posted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T17:49:18-07:00","id":1506680,"title":"","content":"If my friend finds out I got a great deal on my laptop, and asks me to hook him up with that kind of deal, he's asking me to get him in touch with the local guy I know that builds great custom computers for low prices, not asking me to make him one on my own.<br /> <br /> I never said Paradox set up anything, I said Paradox could hook Onyx Path up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T18:13:09-07:00","id":1506684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShovelHeart3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506673#post1506673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I enjoyed all of the visual novel games, but you're right. At least Bloodlines is still a classic that regularly gets covered by YTers and such. I really hope they don't drop the ball on Bloodlines 2......</div> </div> </div> </div>They say that have a lot of red flags in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T18:25:12-07:00","id":1506685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506480-icv2-fall-2022-vtm-comes-4th?p=1506680#post1506680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my friend finds out I got a great deal on my laptop, and asks me to hook him up with that kind of deal, he's asking me to get him in touch with the local guy I know that builds great custom computers for low prices, not asking me to make him one on my own.<br /> <br /> I never said Paradox set up anything, I said Paradox could hook Onyx Path up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure they see it like that. I completely agree with you - Paradox actually coordinating its licensees and helping them do what they are best at would only strengthen the brand. However, they seem to be mostly hands off and not very keen on crossing the streams. I think Exalted is getting a pass primarily because they don't have anything else to do with it now. It's too bonkers to go for a computer game, it's too fringe to go for a mainstream appeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T19:08:14-07:00","id":1506687,"title":"","content":"I don't think Paradox is going to do it either. I was just explaining what I felt the content and context of my earlier post was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heav